  "key": "causes",
  "exact_meaning": true,
  "same_direction": true,
  "reason": "The intended fact states 'Neuroglandular junctions transmit signals to glands to regulate their secretory activity.' The label is 'transmit signals to regulate'. In the available relations, 'causes' defines that SOURCE causally produces the event TARGET. Here, the source (junctions) causes the event (transmission/regulation). The qualifier 'to regulate' describes the nature of the signal/event caused. Other relations like 'enables' imply permission without production, which contradicts the active transmission described. 'has_participant' would make the gland a participant in the transmission, but the regulation is the outcome/cause of the junction's action on the gland. Thus, 'causes' best captures the causal link where the junction initiates the regulatory signal."
